<title>FRANCE: Union boss urges widening of French truck strike.</title>
<headline>Union boss urges widening of French truck strike.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The secretary general of the Communist-led CGT union urged wider strikes on Tuesday to increase the leverage of France's striking truckers, saying a victory for them would be a victory for all.</p>
<p>A spread of the strike movement &quot;is necessary to exert the maximum pressure...and to expand the consciousness in the working world of the intransigence of the transport bosses that is an intransigence we find everywhere,&quot; CGT boss Louis Viannet told France 3 television.</p>
<p>&quot;Workers need to...exert pressure together and say to themselves, if the truckers win, we'll all be stronger tomorrow,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
